    "lines": [
      {
        "scene": "hook",
        "text": "Tamagotchi could die in your pocket, and kids still lined up to own one.",
        "start": 0.3,
        "seconds": 2.84,
        "window": 3.5,
        "fill": 0.811
      },
      {
        "scene": "launch",
        "text": "Bandai put it on sale in Japan in November 1996. In eight months, Japan bought about 10M of them.",
        "start": 3.8,
        "seconds": 5.39,
        "window": 6.03,
        "fill": 0.894
      },
      {
        "scene": "trick",
        "text": "The trick was the pet inside. It got hungry, it got sick, and if you forgot it, it died.",
        "start": 9.83,
        "seconds": 4.0,
        "window": 4.67,
        "fill": 0.857
      },
      {
        "scene": "question",
        "text": "Crazes like that fade fast. So why didn't this one?",
        "start": 14.5,
        "seconds": 2.35,
        "window": 3.03,
        "fill": 0.776
      },
      {
        "scene": "versions",
        "text": "Bandai kept bringing it back in new shapes, with colour screens and new pets to raise.",
        "start": 17.53,
        "seconds": 3.32,
        "window": 4.0,
        "fill": 0.83
      },
      {
        "scene": "world",
        "text": "And it left Japan. By Bandai's count, 51% of all of them went to buyers outside the country.",
        "start": 21.53,
        "seconds": 4.45,
        "window": 5.07,
        "fill": 0.878
      },
      {
        "scene": "payoff",
        "text": "By July last year, Bandai had shipped 100M Tamagotchis. A pet that dies, and still sells.",
        "start": 26.6,
        "seconds": 4.62,
        "window": 5.3,
        "fill": 0.872
      },
      {
        "scene": "ending",
        "text": "Fed it on time, or let it die: which kid were you? Either way, it was a Tamagotchi.",
        "start": 31.9,
        "seconds": 3.6,
        "window": 4.23,
        "fill": 0.851
      }
    ]
  },
